  "Question": "Each side of triangle \\(ABC\\) is \\(12\\) units. \\(D\\) is the foot of the perpendicular dropped from \\(A\\) on \\(BC,\\) and \\(E\\) is the midpoint of \\(AD.\\) The length of \\(BE,\\) in the same unit, is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\sqrt{18}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\sqrt{28}\\)",
    "C": "\\(6\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\sqrt{63}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\sqrt{98}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Since \\(AB=AC\\), the altitude \\(AD\\) also bisects the base \\(BC\\). Hence \\(BD=12/2=6\\). The two right triangles \\(ABD\\) and \\(BDE\\) let us find \\(BE\\) in stages.\n\nIn right triangle \\(ABD\\), the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\\[\nAD^2=AB^2-BD^2=12^2-6^2=108.\n\\]\nBecause \\(E\\) is the midpoint of \\(AD\\),\n\\[\nDE^2=\\left(\\frac{AD}{2}\\right)^2=\\frac{108}{4}=27.\n\\]\nAlso \\(DE\\perp BD\\), so applying the theorem to triangle \\(BDE\\) yields\n\\[\nBE^2=BD^2+DE^2=36+27=63.\n\\]\nA length is positive, so \\(BE=\\sqrt{63}\\) units, choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
